# Build and Test

Read the authorized task scope from the conversation or operator-provided input,
`docs/VERIFICATION.md`, and starting `git status --short`. Confirm the changed
files and modules remain inside the authorized scope. For installed routing, run
`scripts/select_checks.py` for each changed path to produce a deterministic
candidate list. Review its evidence and task authorization before executing
anything; selection itself never authorizes or runs commands (`VERIFY-01`). A
declared L1 implementation authorizes verified, non-mutating, scope-relevant
checks; L2-L4 use their approved command set. Run
the smallest authorized relevant check, then required target/suite,
consumer/contract, and build checks.

Use only verified repository commands and record their evidence. Prefer
non-mutating check or dry-run modes. Do not install tools, run an unapproved
mutating formatter, change signing/dependencies/configuration, clean user files,
or edit production code merely to make verification pass unless the user
explicitly expands the task.

Separate implementation failures from environment failures. Build does not
replace tests. For cross-module or public-contract changes, require applicable
consumer, compatibility, and integration evidence. Finish with
`git diff --check` and relevant diff/status comparison.

Report command, scope, pass/fail/not-run, decisive error, manual checks, and residual risk. State completion only when every required check passes.
